    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `title` / `salutation` feature on the owner endpoints. Since this project generates its DTOs from `openapi.yml` at build time and serves REST via OfficeFloor function pipelines, the change spans the spec, entity, DB schema, and mapper:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`**\n   - Added `title` as an optional input field on `OwnerFields` (MR/MRS/MS/DR).\n   - Added `salutation` as a `readOnly` output field on `Owner`.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter, so the supplied title survives from `POST /api/owners` through to `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `title` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres), and fixed the hsqldb `data.sql` positional seed inserts to include a NULL for the new column (the other data files use named-column inserts and needed no change).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 `title` maps automatically by name; added a derived `salutation` expression: `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present, otherwise just `lastName`.\n\nNo `@RestController` or `@Transactional` were introduced \u2014 the existing OfficeFloor pipeline (`BuildOwner` \u2192 `SaveOwner`) already carries the whole request body through, so `title` flows into the entity with no new pipeline step, and `salutation` is computed at response-mapping time like the other derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, etc.).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (title `DR`, lastName `who` \u2192 salutation `\"DR who\"`) passes, and the full suite reports `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
